## Why This Is Asked
Tests for per-user feature flags are common in SaaS apps. This question checks the ability to seed data, perform API-driven state changes, and verify UI behavior across login and page reloads in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Per-user feature flags and API seed/reset
- End-to-end UI verification of dynamic layouts
- Test isolation and deterministic CI runs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example using Playwright-like syntax (pseudocode)
// seedUser(), setFlag(), login() are helper utilities
test('compact dashboard toggling', async ({ page, request }) => {
  const { userId, email, password } = await seedUser(request);
  await setFlag(request, userId, 'CompactDashboard', true);
  await login(page, email, password);
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-compact')).toBeVisible();
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-compact')).toBeVisible();
  await setFlag(request, userId, 'CompactDashboard', false);
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-full')).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you guard against flaky UI assertions caused by caching?
- How would you extend the test to cover multiple user segments (roles/regions) and parallel execution?

